nfidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Andy Ogles (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tennessee's 5th District is an open Republican-held seat after Andy Ogles lost renomination, with Republican Charlie Hatcher facing Democrat Chaz Molder in November. The district leans Republican by about ten points, and nearly every expert rater calls the race Safe or Solid for Republicans, with only a couple rating it Likely R. A late-August poll of likely voters showed Hatcher ahead by eight points, and prediction markets give Molder roughly an 8% chance.\nMolder has out-raised Hatcher by a wide margin and holds a large cash advantage, and he has been on air with an ad push, while Hatcher has drawn some negative coverage tied to a Columbia property investigation. Still, the structural Republican lean in this Nashville-area district makes an upset a steep climb, and the race is best characterized as Likely Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.079, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0675, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0985, "margin": -9.0}]}